    <string name="help_title">Help</string>
    <string name="help_body">1. The bottom buttons open Help, Application skin, and About Us.\n\n2. Add Audio selects an MP3 soundtrack. It is optional for pictures-only silent videos, single-video repeat exports, and joining multiple videos.\n\n3. Add Video/Image selects one picture, multiple pictures, one short video, or multiple videos. Numbered picture and video names are sorted in numeric order. Supported picture inputs include JPG, PNG, WEBP, HEIC, and HEIF.\n\n4. The Loaded media list replaces the old status panel. It shows the selected pictures or videos directly on the main screen. Long-press a drag handle to reorder items before merging, duplicate an item to use it more than once, or remove an item from the edit.\n\n5. Merge To Video opens export settings, then asks where to save the final MP4.\n\n6. Export settings support 720p or 1080p, Vertical or Horizontal video direction, 30 fps or 60 fps, Image time, and Video repeats. With MP3 plus pictures, 0 sec keeps the first picture for the whole song. 1-60 sec rotates pictures in the arranged order and loops them until the MP3 ends. If Automatically split time is checked while Image time is 0, the MP3 length is divided equally across all selected pictures. For pictures without MP3, Image time must be 1-60 sec and the output is a silent video with length equal to picture count times image time. For one video without MP3, Video repeats creates a new video where that video plays the selected number of times and shows the estimated total length before export. Multi-picture and multi-video exports are merged internally in the arranged order until one final video remains.\n\n7. Preview shows the selected visual and MP3 playback when audio is selected.\n\n8. The merge progress bar appears above Preview while the final video is created. If merging gets stuck or fails, send Downloads/AVTOHIT/AVTOHIT-debug-log.txt. Every merge appends to the same log file. The app normalizes pictures before FFmpeg, but if a picture still cannot be decoded, re-save that picture as JPG or PNG and try again.</string>
